 "title": "The Trail Board Painted at DUSK 🌲",
 "made_for_kids": false,
 "premise": "Every sunrise the trail board at our trailhead paints one short rule for the day, and obeying it pays off. This weekend it painted at dusk, which it never does, telling me not to walk a creek path that is on no map, and at sunrise it repainted itself in four lines to say the opposite: walk it with my sister June so she comes home.",
 "twist": "Nothing is explained. The path is there, June has already seen it, the warden says it isn't theirs and the board has written two rules for the same morning, so the viewer has to pick which board to trust.",
